Never listed: Context Guru's own components and Claude Code's built-in tools (carrying the unused built-ins costs $2.40; you cannot remove them).
'client tool' = a tool declared by the agent that is neither MCP nor a skill (usually one of Claude Code's own newer tools); --disallowedTools hides it for that run.
A server removal takes effect in the next session. `claude mcp remove` takes -s user|project|local; `claude mcp list` shows where each is defined.
